S3: Resource vs Client

Boto3 historically provides two major interfaces:

Client:
Low-level AWS service API.
s3 = boto3.client("s3")

Resource:
Higher-level object-oriented interface for some services.
s3 = boto3.resource("s3")

Example:

bucket = s3.Bucket("my-bucket")
for obj in bucket.objects.all():
    print(obj.key)

Modern Boto3 work often uses clients, particularly when you need precise API control.

A good beginner rule:
Learn client first. Learn resource afterward.
